  "final_message": "I wrote `answer.json` with four functions whose own code emits `subscription.updated`, all in `billing/subscriptions.py`:\n\n- `subscriptions.transition` emits it for every status change except to `canceled`, where it emits `subscription.canceled` instead.\n- `subscriptions.change_items` emits it after the items are replaced.\n- `subscriptions.cancel` emits it when the cancellation is scheduled for period end (`at_period_end`).\n- `subscriptions.reactivate` emits it when a scheduled cancellation is undone.\n\n`pause`, `resume` and the dunning code's `record_failure` also produce the event, but only by calling `transition`, so I left them out. No other module in `billing` emits that event type. I found this by searching the code and reading the emitters, and I didn't run the tests.",
